# nr-office-formula-lib-financial

## Registration (lead-owned functions/mod.rs)

Add `mod financial;` after the existing library module declarations.
Append `financial::FUNCTIONS,` to TABLES, preserving other tasks' entries.
The table contains all 33 Financial-category exported paths discovered from the
installed @formulajs/formulajs 4.6.1 namespace. Its actual exports end at XNPV;
YIELD*, ACCRINTM and the other absent spreadsheet names mentioned by the plan are
not exports or stubs in this installed version and are not fabricated here.

No new crate or Cargo edge. Existing coerce, mixdog-js V8 math and radix helpers
are reused. Calendar prerequisites, resolved from the production registry:
YEARFRAC, DATEDIF, DAYS360, DAYS (owned by nr-office-formula-lib-text-date).
Register those before financial_calendar_results_equal_original_bits. The pure
financial test needs no datetime table. Neither test silently skips a missing
function; together they cover every normal recorded output.

Remove the ignore attribute from financial_exports_are_registered_in_the_production_library
when the production table is wired. twin_live_financial stays opt-in because it
runs Node and the bounded nontermination diagnostic.

## Source and output coverage

Implementation: mixdog-xlsx-formula/src/functions/financial.rs
Original: node_modules/@formulajs/formulajs/lib/esm/index.mjs, 11473-13050,
plus validDate/ensureDate/lastCoupDateBeforeSettlement immediately before it.
Recorder enumerates Financial JSDoc function identities against the actual export
namespace and traverses nested aliases, rejecting any unhandled export.

Recorded 3,331 returning cases, all 33 exports, original Node 22.20.0.
Each case preserves float bits (NaN/sign/payload included), Error identity label,
throw message, undefined/null/arrays/dates and time zone. No tolerance or NaN
normalization. Numeric/date inputs are encoded before calling the mutation-prone
reference. Dates include UTC, America/New_York and Asia/Seoul. Coverage includes
missing arguments, truthy vs undefined defaults, bad types, multiple errors,
raw/string CUM periods, nonfinite values where the original terminates,
DB's toFixed(3), scientific-notation parseInt conversions, all day-count bases,
COUPDAYS overflowed month ends, IRR/RATE/XIRR guesses and cashflow shapes.

Node command (executed, reference read-only, outputs only owned fixtures):
node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-financial.mjs --tree C:/Project/mixdog --write
Without --write the recorder emits JSON and does not change fixtures.
Index office-financial/MANIFEST.json in the root fixture manifest. It carries the
source SHA-256, exact export roster, case count and golden byte/hash metadata.

Strict tests:
- every_original_financial_export_has_one_body
